A||||2||Scott2M4||Steering column moves/front end feels loose||||5
Z||000000||Scott2M4||11-02-1999||09:44 PM||||By holding the steering wheel on my '87 and moving from left to right or top to bottom, the steering column can be moved about 1/2".<P>Also, the front end feels loose.  The car tracks nicely but clunks when hitting bumps.<P>I'm not a mechanic (though I plan to become one very soon - now that I've acquired a toy!).  Can someone tell me what these problems sound like?  Are they related?  Does the loose front end sound like a problem with the steering rack?  Does that mean $$$?<P>Any help is GREATLY appreciated!||||reg||5
Z||000001||lowCG||11-03-1999||03:00 AM||||There's another,very recent post on the steering column problem,and the front end could be many things,including the steering rack,but you need to start at the wheels and look for slop.Try grabbing the top of the tire,on the ground,and pull back and forth.If you feel anything clunking,that's the wheel bearings.The reason I recomend doing this not on a jack,in the air,is that a bearing can check out good this way,but will be sloppy while loaded.<BR>Could also be Balljoints,control arm bushings,shocks,or a combination.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Scott2M4||11-03-1999||06:05 AM||||Sorry, folks.  After posting this question, I saw the other post in the tech section regarding the column problem.<P>I'll be better about this in the future.||||reg||4
